  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.4: User-delegation SAS. GetUserDelegationSasUriAsync and GetSasUriAsync sign with a delegation key from Microsoft Entra ID, so SAS URIs now work under a managed identity or any other token credential rather than requiring a shared account key; the key is cached and refreshed near expiry, and CanGenerateSasUri reports whether a service SAS is possible. Service endpoints are configurable via EndpointSuffix and explicit BlobServiceUri/TableServiceUri/QueueServiceUri, which is what lets a token-credential client target the Azurite emulator. BlobBridge gains SAS-async, GetAttachmentProperties, ranged download, SetAttachmentHttpHeaders, and a content-type argument on the attach methods. New SetHttpHeadersAsync on IBlobRepository stamps content type and disposition on an existing blob without clearing the other headers. Content disposition supports inline rendering and is now signed into the SAS - previously it was appended to the query after signing, which produced a URI the service rejected. CancellationToken added throughout the blob API. Breaking: UploadFileAsync gained a contentType parameter in third position, matching UploadAsync. v1.3: Added TypedQueueListener<T>, a BackgroundService that drives an IQueueMessageHandler<T> per message with a polling loop, per-message elapsed-time logging, release-on-failure retry, and poison handling on top of TypedQueueClient<T>. RunOnceAsync supports single-message or drain-until-empty passes for triggered/one-shot hosts such as Azure Container Apps jobs. Register with AddQueueListener<T, THandler>. v1.2: Merged the former Benday.BlobStorage package into Benday.AzureStorage; BlobBridge now lives in the Benday.AzureStorage.Blobs namespace. Also includes blob repositories, Table Storage repositories, typed queue clients, queue health checks, and DI helpers.",
